# HomeNetWatch

UXI-style home network monitoring: Pi remote agents push staged test results to FastAPI + Postgres; React dashboard reads APIs only.

## Architecture

- Remote agent → server (ingest); browser → dashboard → server (read). The remote agent never talks to the dashboard.
- Stack: FastAPI / Postgres / React+Vite+TS / TanStack Query / **Recharts**.
- No Grafana in this product. The remote agent package posts device health; staged tests stay out until asked.

## Repo layout

- `SPEC.md` — source of truth
- `server/` — FastAPI app, models, migrations, seed, tests
- `dashboard/` — Vite React UI
- `monitor/` — Pi package (setup page, enroll, device health)
- `docker-compose.yml` — db + server + dashboard

## Conventions

- Conventional commits: `docs:`, `feat:`, `test:`, `fix:`, `chore:`
- Idempotent seed under `server` (stable IDs / wipe demo org)
- Cookie auth: `admin` (write) / `viewer` (read-only UI)
- Prefer thin APIs; rollups can be raw metrics until later phases
- Charts: Recharts only for this slice

## Out of scope unless asked

Staged test runner, Wi-Fi/RF pages, webhooks, full enrollment ETag matrix, Playwright journeys, Grafana.
